   "evidence": "Domain.lean:182 docstring states it: \"Positivity of `P\u00b7q` is not assumed: `Q\u00b2 > 0` together with either side already forces it\", and Domain.lean:198-199 derives it (`have h2pq : 0 < 2 * g K.p K.q := hQ.trans_le h1`). Domain.lean:240-241 passes only `h.q2_pos`, `h.q2_le_two_p_dot_q`, `h.p_dot_q_le_p_dot_k`. Grep for `BasicAssumptions` shows a single `where`-construction, at Polarized/Kinematics.lean:308.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Kinematics/Bounds.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the `p_dot_q_pos` and `p_dot_k_pos` fields, keeping `q2_pos`, `q2_le_two_p_dot_q`, `p_dot_q_le_p_dot_k`, and re-expose them as lemmas `BasicAssumptions.p_dot_q_pos` / `BasicAssumptions.p_dot_k_pos` so `xBj_in_unitInterval` and `yInel_in_unitInterval` are unchanged. The only construction site is `basicAssumptions_kPol` (Polarized/Kinematics.lean:308), so the churn is one declaration.",
   "issue": "`BasicAssumptions` carries two redundant obligations: `p_dot_q_pos` follows from `q2_pos` and `q2_le_two_p_dot_q` (`0 < Q\u00b2 \u2264 2 P\u00b7q`), and `p_dot_k_pos` then follows from `p_dot_q_le_p_dot_k`. The PR rewrote every lemma in this file to minimal hypotheses and `BasicAssumptions.invariants_mem_kinematicDomain` (Domain.lean:238) uses only three of the five fields, so the bundle now demands strictly more of a user than any consumer needs.",
   "line": 33
  }
